Testing and local session state
-------------------------------
  - Started Civil 3D 2027 Metric and opened the blank Drawing1.dwg. The existing
    ChatGPT/Codex MCP entry returned drawing information from that session.
  - The Release build finished with zero warnings and zero errors.
  - The stdio smoke suite passed in standard, split, and read-only modes.
  - Both modes of the rebuilt executable read the live drawing and disconnected
    cleanly. Read-only mode rejected drawing edits and SewerGEMS imports.
  - The installer was tested in temporary directories. It generated valid
    Codex TOML and Claude JSON for an installation path with spaces.
  - The live MCP client held dist/C3dMcp/c3d-mcp-server.exe open, so the updated
    build was delivered in dist/C3dMcp-2027.zip. The running client uses the
    previous executable until upgraded. The existing client configuration
    was used for live verification.
  - The Secure MCP Tunnel instructions are included. Cloud activation requires
    a tunnel associated with the user's ChatGPT workspace and was outside the
    live verification performed here.
